{"version": 2, "width": 100, "height": 40, "timestamp": 1794835000, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/sh", "TERM": "xterm-256color"}, "title": "CVE-2026-98260 PoC demo, plain-kernel oops (VulnAtlas Research)"}
[0.0, "o", "=== VulnAtlas Research - CVE-2026-98260 PoC demo, plain (non-KASAN) kernel ===\n"]
[0.25, "o", "=== Linux kernel POSIX per-thread CPU timer UAF (SIGKILL into exec window) ===\n"]
[0.25, "o", "=== crash: rb_next <- timerqueue_del <- posix_cpu_timers_exit <- release_task <- wait4 ===\n"]
[0.3, "o", "# CVE-2026-98260: Sanitized trigger description\n"]
[0.008, "o", "VulnAtlas Research | 2026-11-15\n"]
[0.008, "o", "Pseudocode only: this is not a runnable program and not a working exploit.\n"]
[0.008, "o", "It describes the trigger sequence for the root-cause analysis. The runnable\n"]
[0.008, "o", "lab driver stays private and is available to maintainers on request.\n"]
[0.008, "o", "\n"]
[0.008, "o", "## Trigger sequence\n"]
[0.008, "o", "1. A parent forks a MULTITHREADED child (at least two threads); the parent\n"]
[0.008, "o", "   later waits in wait4() to reap it.\n"]
[0.008, "o", "2. The child's NON-LEADER thread calls timer_create(CLOCK_THREAD_CPUTIME_ID,\n"]
[0.008, "o", "   ...) + timer_settime(): the per-thread CPU timer is what queues the\n"]
[0.008, "o", "   k_itimer's cpu_timer node on THAT thread's posix_cputimers rbtree. Any\n"]
[0.008, "o", "   other clock leaves the node out of that rbtree and the described read\n"]
[0.008, "o", "   becomes impossible.\n"]
[0.008, "o", "   [PSEUDOCODE: timer_create(CLOCK_THREAD_CPUTIME_ID, &sigevent, &timerid);\n"]
[0.008, "o", "    timer_settime(timerid, 0, &its)]\n"]
[0.008, "o", "3. That thread execve()s and the exec is forced to FAIL on a late failure\n"]
[0.008, "o", "   path; the unwind returns -EINTR and a delayed kill lands during the\n"]
[0.008, "o", "   killable exec wait; the unwind then runs through get_signal -> do_exit ->\n"]
[0.008, "o", "   exit_itimers(), which frees the k_itimer while its node is still queued;\n"]
[0.008, "o", "   rcu_core later executes the kmem_cache_free(). A plain exit is NOT a\n"]
[0.008, "o", "   trigger route here: without the failed-exec unwind the path does not\n"]
[0.008, "o", "   reach the bug.\n"]
[0.008, "o", "4. The parent's wait4() reaping runs release_task() ->\n"]
[0.008, "o", "   posix_cpu_timers_exit() -> timerqueue_del(), which reads the timerqueue\n"]
[0.008, "o", "   node of the already-freed k_itimer when reaping lands inside the\n"]
[0.008, "o", "   RCU-free window.\n"]
[0.008, "o", "\n"]
[0.008, "o", "## Race window control\n"]
[0.008, "o", "The observable window is between the child's exit and the RCU grace period\n"]
[0.008, "o", "that executes the deferred free. The lab driver paces reaping with a\n"]
[0.008, "o", "microsecond-scale delay sweep (kill-delay parameter) to land wait4() inside\n"]
[0.008, "o", "that window deterministically. Tuning parameter values stay out of this\n"]
[0.008, "o", "description and remain in the private driver only.\n"]
[0.008, "o", "\n"]
[0.008, "o", "## Scope notes\n"]
[0.008, "o", "- Written as a UAF-read trigger demo; explicitly crash-only scope.\n"]
[0.008, "o", "- No gadget talk, no escalation chain, no exploitation primitives.\n"]
[0.008, "o", "- Config requirements: none beyond default (CONFIG_POSIX_TIMERS=y).\n"]
[0.008, "o", "=== run: rounds=2000 kill=100us groom=15ms spray=800 mode=1 (msgsnd), kernel 6.6.157 non-KASAN ===\n"]
[0.3, "o", "groom cfg: rounds=2000 kill_delay_us=100 groom_ms=15 spray_n=800 mode=1 mark=0x4141414141414141\n"]
[0.0, "o", "round 0 sprayed=816 timeouts=0\n"]
